<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.KOREA'S SEPT RIGHTS OFFERING PLANS SLIGHTLY DOWN.</title>
<headline>S.KOREA'S SEPT RIGHTS OFFERING PLANS SLIGHTLY DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thirteen listed South Korean companies plan 391 billion won worth of rights offerings for payment in September, down slightly from 392.2 billion a year ago, the Korean Listed Companies' Association said on Monday.</p>
<p>The largest offering would be by Hana Bank, which plans to issue 13.33 million new shares for payment by September 25.</p>
<p>The offering would raise the bank's paid-in capital to 233.45 billion won from the current 166.78 billion, the association said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
